{:itonami.blueprint/id "cloud-itonami-unspsc-10"
 :itonami.blueprint/name "Independent Urban Apiary & Pollinator Services"
 :itonami.blueprint/unspsc-segment "10"
 :itonami.blueprint/domain :agriculture/apiary-pollination
 :itonami.blueprint/license "AGPL-3.0-or-later"
 :itonami.blueprint/social-impact [:pollinator-health :urban-biodiversity :local-food-resilience]
 :itonami.blueprint/governor :apiary-operations-governor
 :itonami.blueprint/robotics true
 :itonami.blueprint/required-technologies [:robotics :telemetry :optimization :audit-ledger]
 :itonami.blueprint/status :public-oss
 :itonami.blueprint/maturity :implemented
 :itonami.blueprint/implemented-slice
 "ColonyAdvisor ⊣ Apiary Operations Governor, langgraph-clj StateGraph,
 append-only audit ledger. A pollination-SERVICE operator coordination
 actor (colony-health data logging, pollination-route scheduling
 against customer sites, disease/pest concern flagging, honey/wax
 harvest coordination) -- not direct hive-intervention actuation
 authority and not disease-free/quarantine-clearance certification
 authority. Four ops (`:log-colony-health` / `:schedule-pollination-
 route` / `:flag-disease-concern` / `:coordinate-harvest`), all
 `:effect :propose` only. Twelve concrete governor checks elaborate
 this blueprint's four HARD invariants: propose-only effect, closed op
 allowlist, closed proposal-effect allowlist (no direct hive-
 intervention actuation), permanent hive-actuate block, permanent
 disease-free/quarantine-certification-authority block, independent
 site verification/registration before route scheduling, independent
 hive verification/registration before harvest coordination,
 independent cumulative harvest-quantity recompute against the hive's
 own logged sustainable-harvest ceiling, double-schedule guard, queen-
 status validation, weight plausibility validation, and temperature
 plausibility validation. Disease/pest-concern flagging (grounded in
 WOAH Terrestrial Animal Health Code Chapter 9.2 notifiable bee
 diseases) ALWAYS escalates to a human apiary coordinator;
 `:log-colony-health` is the only op eligible to auto-commit, and only
 at phase 3 when governor-clean. See docs/adr/0001-architecture.md
 Decision 0 for this blueprint's documented governor-keyword overlap
 with `cloud-itonami-isco-6123` (a different, independent
 implementation of the same domain from the occupation-classification
 axis)."}
